WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:02:13.387 --> 00:02:14.669
<i>Ground control,</i>


00:02:14.693 --> 00:02:16.785
<i>Vesta 1 leaving chasing mode.</i>


00:02:16.916 --> 00:02:19.921
<i>Navicon calculating approh
for final docking maneuver.</i>


00:02:21.358 --> 00:02:24.147
<i>- Affirmative.
- Continue approach.</i>


00:02:24.278 --> 00:02:27.633
<i>Entering on final
docking corridor.</i>


00:02:27.764 --> 00:02:30.943
<i>Rubikon has received Navicon
data.</i>


00:02:31.073 --> 00:02:33.906
Ready for last docking phase.


00:02:34.037 --> 00:02:36.694
80 centimeters of
sturdy insulation.


00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:38.874
5 centimeters of reinforced glass.


00:02:39.004 --> 00:02:41.268
80 centimeters of sturdy
insulation.


00:02:41.399 --> 00:02:42.683
- 5 centimeters...
- Who would have thought


00:02:42.707 --> 00:02:44.667
space travel means doing nothing
but...


00:02:44.798 --> 00:02:47.063
...Staring at monitors.


00:02:47.194 --> 00:02:48.588
...Reinforced glass.


00:02:48.719 --> 00:02:51.551
80 centimeters
of sturdy insulation.


00:02:51.681 --> 00:02:54.251
5 centimeters
of reinforced glass.


00:02:54.381 --> 00:02:57.214
Relax.


00:02:57.345 --> 00:02:58.782
I am relaxed.


00:02:58.913 --> 00:03:00.438
What makes you think
I'm not relaxed?


00:03:00.569 --> 00:03:01.962
I'm relaxed.


00:03:06.363 --> 00:03:08.323
Uh, is it meant to do that?


00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:12.680
Isn't it supposed to,
you know, hold my body weight?


00:03:17.036 --> 00:03:21.174
Yeah. You're relaxed.
I can see that.


00:03:21.305 --> 00:03:24.355
See. If you press here,
and then it comes off.


00:03:24.486 --> 00:03:26.403
Yeah, but I didn't press
any button.


00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:27.797
It just came off on its own.


00:03:27.927 --> 00:03:29.062
We'll be fine.


00:03:29.192 --> 00:03:31.370
<i>Commander Wagner.</i>


00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:34.855
This is Rubikon.
What is your current position?


00:03:34.986 --> 00:03:40.519
<i>Navicon indicates range
350 meters and grade 3.5.</i>


00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.351
- 350?
- I'm reading 150 meters here.


00:03:46.443 --> 00:03:50.233
They're way too fast
for their position.


00:03:50.364 --> 00:03:52.761
Wagner, we got you at 150.


00:03:52.891 --> 00:03:55.416
<b>350 or 150,</b>


00:03:55.547 --> 00:03:57.204
<i>the station should be inside
by now,</i>


00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.121
but we have no visual contact.


00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.696
- Where is it?
- I knew it.


00:04:03.826 --> 00:04:05.699
<i>- Vesta 1...
- I fucking knew it.</i>


00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:06.894
<i>Connection to Navicon
seems flawed.</i>


00:04:06.918 --> 00:04:08.705
<i>Reboot so we get control again.</i>


00:04:08.836 --> 00:04:11.233
Affirmative.


00:04:11.363 --> 00:04:12.670
Uh, Hannah?


00:04:14.195 --> 00:04:15.502
What the fuck?


00:04:18.376 --> 00:04:19.903
Shit! We see it now.


00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.995
The station
is about 90 meters away.


00:04:23.125 --> 00:04:24.477
<i>I'm switching to manual mode.</i>


00:04:24.608 --> 00:04:27.090
<i>Negative. Flying manually
is prohibited.</i>


00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.070
The thing they told us
never to touch, brilliant.


00:04:29.094 --> 00:04:31.447
I need to take over or we might
get hit by the sails.


00:04:31.577 --> 00:04:33.581
<i>Wagner. Leave it to the A.I..</i>


00:04:33.712 --> 00:04:36.892
<i>The company wants
no risk of human error.</i>


00:04:37.023 --> 00:04:37.807
Hannah.


00:04:37.938 --> 00:04:39.114
Hannah! Hannah! Watch out!


00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.208
No! No!


00:04:54.188 --> 00:04:57.500
- That was close.
- Yeah, too close.


00:04:57.629 --> 00:04:59.372
Initializing reverse thrusters.


00:04:59.503 --> 00:05:01.115
<i>Okay. At own discretion.</i>


00:05:01.246 --> 00:05:02.335
Okay.


00:05:04.166 --> 00:05:06.692
<i>Okay, um...</i>


00:05:09.654 --> 00:05:11.266
Speeding down
for contact capture.


00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.188
Slowing down.


00:05:15.318 --> 00:05:16.559
We got you on the monitors now.


00:05:16.625 --> 00:05:19.063
<i>Alright, 2.2...</i>


00:05:19.194 --> 00:05:20.414
<i>2.1...</i>


00:05:20.545 --> 00:05:22.331
Wagner, your rate is stil
too high.


00:05:22.462 --> 00:05:23.725
Yes.


00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.382
You better tell everyone
to hold on.


00:05:25.512 --> 00:05:26.688
Oh, Father.


00:05:26.819 --> 00:05:30.085
Wait. 1.9...


00:05:30.216 --> 00:05:31.219
Okay, I'm on target.


00:05:32.438 --> 00:05:33.484
Steady.


00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.759
- Steadier.
- Left.


00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:42.023
More left!


00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.373
<i>Alright, in parking position.</i>


00:06:04.503 --> 00:06:06.072
<i>Well done, Wagner.</i>


00:06:06.203 --> 00:06:08.468
<i>Activating hooks
to finish procedure.</i>


00:06:17.486 --> 00:06:19.403
Connecting to station's
gravitation field.


00:06:27.898 --> 00:06:29.423
See?


00:06:32.036 --> 00:06:34.563
- What the fuck was that?
- Navicon was completely off.


00:06:34.695 --> 00:06:36.219
But it was not our fault.


00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.677
Nibra cannot blame us
for that, right?


00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:40.315
The station's readings
were right.


00:06:40.446 --> 00:06:41.622
Good.


00:06:45.411 --> 00:06:46.761
Wait a second.


00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:53.036
Wait.


00:06:53.166 --> 00:06:55.475
She's a soldier.


00:06:55.605 --> 00:06:57.566
Why would Nibra send a soldier?


00:07:05.102 --> 00:07:07.716
- Welcome to the Rubikon.
- Commander Wagner,


00:07:07.848 --> 00:07:09.983
Dr. Abbott,
glad to have you on board.


00:07:10.113 --> 00:07:11.571
What just happened,
Commander Jensen?


00:07:11.595 --> 00:07:14.165
Can you explain?


00:07:14.295 --> 00:07:16.516
The error must have happened
on ground control's end.


00:07:16.648 --> 00:07:19.480
Navicon somehow lost
a connection to your shuttle


00:07:19.611 --> 00:07:21.484
without a notification.


00:07:21.615 --> 00:07:24.273
Do you know why?


00:07:24.404 --> 00:07:27.495
Tracy will look into it
immediately.


00:07:27.626 --> 00:07:29.718
And bring me the report
once you're done.


00:07:34.075 --> 00:07:35.818
The crew cabins?


00:07:35.948 --> 00:07:38.911
Yes. Um, follow me, please.


00:07:46.404 --> 00:07:48.581
I hope you'll be satisfied
with your cabin.


00:07:48.712 --> 00:07:50.674
It's not much, but you get
the biggest one we got.


00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:53.722
- Oh, no, please don't.
- That's really not necessary.


00:07:53.853 --> 00:07:55.422
I hope your dad's okay
about that.


00:07:55.553 --> 00:07:57.426
Why? Did he ask for that?


00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:02.557
Um...


00:09:39.674 --> 00:09:40.938
To the new crew.


00:09:41.069 --> 00:09:43.554
May you and the three others
arriving on Friday


00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:45.207
have a good time


00:09:45.338 --> 00:09:47.648
and a productive work experience
together.


00:09:49.478 --> 00:09:50.654
Hmm.


00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:01.197
So, I... I-I hear
you're a chemist.


00:10:01.328 --> 00:10:03.724
Yes, but I've read
all of your reports, and...


00:10:03.855 --> 00:10:05.335
Sure, that's all you
need to conduct


00:10:05.465 --> 00:10:10.737
complex gene modification.
I am sure you will do great.


00:10:10.868 --> 00:10:13.830
As long as you can
follow orders.


00:10:13.961 --> 00:10:16.182
My words exactly.


00:10:16.313 --> 00:10:20.191
Commander, I heard about your
excellent navigational skills.


00:10:20.322 --> 00:10:21.759
Thank you.


00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.894
And I heard a lot
about you, too, Doctor.


00:10:24.024 --> 00:10:25.899
Yeah, hopefully
only good things.


00:10:26.028 --> 00:10:27.029
Yeah.


00:10:29.558 --> 00:10:31.258
Commander, it's the laser comm.


00:10:33.436 --> 00:10:36.441
- Please enjoy the party.
- It's still my shift.


00:10:39.752 --> 00:10:43.413
How about we play one last game?


00:10:43.543 --> 00:10:45.939
Let's show the new ones
how it's done.


00:10:46.069 --> 00:10:47.462
Come on, new ones.


00:10:52.212 --> 00:10:53.998
Sure. What are the stakes?


00:10:54.129 --> 00:10:56.526
- Debit points.
- Okay.


00:11:07.155 --> 00:11:08.984
- Danilo.
- Uh-huh?


00:11:09.114 --> 00:11:10.354
If you can give Commander Wagner


00:11:10.378 --> 00:11:11.904
a piece of cake, please.


00:11:12.034 --> 00:11:13.210
Thank you.


00:11:13.341 --> 00:11:17.786
Sorry, Commander.
My son takes this whole...


00:11:17.917 --> 00:11:21.663
being called off thing
a bit personally.


00:11:21.793 --> 00:11:23.188
And what about you?


00:11:23.318 --> 00:11:26.935
I just want to see
what type of a game you play.


00:11:27.065 --> 00:11:28.504
Oh, I got 7.


00:11:28.634 --> 00:11:30.462
- I'll take one.
- No, make it two.


00:11:32.641 --> 00:11:35.342
Up to your liking?


00:11:35.473 --> 00:11:37.104
They are probably used
to different standards


00:11:37.128 --> 00:11:38.741
in the air domes, right?


00:11:38.872 --> 00:11:41.179
Well, if you want


00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:43.357
your essential amino acids
and minerals covered,


00:11:43.488 --> 00:11:44.839
that's all you get, I'm afraid.


00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.451
Sorry, domer boy.


00:11:46.582 --> 00:11:49.676
Hey, what's your problem?


00:11:49.807 --> 00:11:51.286
Nothing.


00:11:51.417 --> 00:11:53.160
I just wonder what makes
an executive's son


00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:54.685
want to come
to a place like this.


00:11:54.816 --> 00:11:57.865
- Danilo.
- You think I chose to come here?


00:11:57.996 --> 00:11:59.652
To this old piece of junk?


00:11:59.782 --> 00:12:01.787
So then Daddy is punishing you?


00:12:01.918 --> 00:12:03.791
Why?


00:12:03.922 --> 00:12:05.882
Did you misbehave?


00:12:06.014 --> 00:12:07.277
Is that my piece?


00:12:08.714 --> 00:12:09.934
Thank you.


00:12:13.549 --> 00:12:16.207
Commander Wagner?


00:12:23.221 --> 00:12:24.527
What is that?


00:12:24.658 --> 00:12:26.227
It's our new flight route
for tomorrow.


00:12:26.357 --> 00:12:28.841
What? Why did they change it?


00:12:28.972 --> 00:12:31.324
There's strange fog across
the northern hemisphere.


00:12:31.455 --> 00:12:35.114
Nobody knows what it is.
Over Ostgrunden territory.


00:12:35.245 --> 00:12:37.118
Wait, Ostgrunden?


00:12:37.249 --> 00:12:40.124
Yes,
and there have been fatalities.


00:12:40.256 --> 00:12:43.000
What? W-What happened?


00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.134
They can't tell yet.


00:12:45.265 --> 00:12:46.678
Isn't Ostgrunden
where they arrested


00:12:46.702 --> 00:12:48.576
those Green Fighter activists?


00:12:48.707 --> 00:12:52.193
Were the victims,
the Green Fighters?


00:12:52.323 --> 00:12:53.892
There were a few hundred.


00:13:00.077 --> 00:13:02.605
But they said they can
circumnavigate you


00:13:02.736 --> 00:13:04.043
around it, right?


00:13:04.173 --> 00:13:06.002
It'll take us half a day longer.


00:13:06.133 --> 00:13:08.834
Okay. Looks good, sir.


00:13:08.966 --> 00:13:11.012
- Tomorrow evening, as planned.
- Okay.


00:13:27.523 --> 00:13:29.354
Come on, give me something.


00:13:32.054 --> 00:13:34.974
You know we're not really
supposed to be in here, right?


00:13:38.024 --> 00:13:39.545
I can't find anything
on the Internet.


00:13:39.591 --> 00:13:41.553
There's nothing on the cameras.


00:13:41.683 --> 00:13:43.905
So I thought I'd try this.


00:13:44.036 --> 00:13:46.738
So. That's it?


00:13:46.869 --> 00:13:50.918
This atmosphere-analyzing thing
that never worked?


00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:53.925
Can't even get it to budge.


00:13:54.056 --> 00:13:55.363
You could have asked me.


00:13:55.494 --> 00:13:58.151
- I'm in contact with Nibra.
- Right.


00:13:58.281 --> 00:14:01.244
As if I believe a single word
a government company says.


00:14:01.374 --> 00:14:03.074
Come on. They're not the enemy.


00:14:03.205 --> 00:14:05.906
Uh, yes, actually,
yes, they are.


00:14:06.036 --> 00:14:08.346
Of course, not if you work
for them.


00:14:12.005 --> 00:14:13.703
You worry for your friends, huh?


00:14:25.729 --> 00:14:27.210
You're good.


00:14:44.374 --> 00:14:47.860
All systems are online and
crowd control gave the final go.


00:14:47.991 --> 00:14:50.865
- You guys are ready?
- Yes, we are.


00:14:50.996 --> 00:14:53.479
And the samples?


00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.179
- Dad.
- Hm?


00:14:55.309 --> 00:14:56.703
The samples.


00:14:56.833 --> 00:14:57.966
Yeah, of course.


00:15:01.104 --> 00:15:03.020
And these mother cultures
will endure


00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:04.432
the extended flight time, right?


00:15:04.545 --> 00:15:05.677
- Of course.
- Of course.


00:15:05.808 --> 00:15:07.159
Yes.


00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:08.509
Yeah.


00:15:09.861 --> 00:15:12.866
That's our slot. Let's go.


00:15:12.997 --> 00:15:15.350
Commander Wagner.


00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.239
Bye-bye.


00:16:13.815 --> 00:16:15.794
The son is on the way now
with the mother cultures,


00:16:15.818 --> 00:16:19.652
but I'm pretty sure they've been
manipulated as well.


00:16:19.783 --> 00:16:22.877
<i>Well, there's been
a change of plans.</i>


00:16:23.007 --> 00:16:24.663
<i>The committee decided</i>


00:16:24.794 --> 00:16:26.665
<i>that we want to move on
to Icarus sooner.</i>


00:16:26.797 --> 00:16:29.324
Already? When?


00:16:29.455 --> 00:16:31.285
<i>Apparently,
in the next few days.</i>


00:16:31.415 --> 00:16:33.812
<i>What? But I haven't been able
to investigate</i>


00:16:33.942 --> 00:16:35.729
<i>in the algae's breathing cycle.</i>


00:16:35.859 --> 00:16:37.620
<i>Then you have to search
faster to make it on time.</i>


00:16:37.644 --> 00:16:40.607
If he finds out,
he might destroy samples.


00:16:40.738 --> 00:16:44.050
<i>Prepare Icarus unnoticed, then.</i>


00:16:44.181 --> 00:16:45.619
Look...


00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:47.753
The station seems more
interwoven with the algae


00:16:47.883 --> 00:16:50.280
than anticipated.


00:16:50.411 --> 00:16:51.693
It could be more complicated
to just...


00:16:51.717 --> 00:16:54.462
<i>Wagner.
Just prepare Icarus.</i>


00:17:59.593 --> 00:18:01.248
Hope you know that some of them


00:18:01.379 --> 00:18:03.774
were just exposed to high levels
of cosmic radiation.


00:18:03.906 --> 00:18:06.432
I got instructed on them
very thoroughly.


00:18:06.563 --> 00:18:07.914
Oh, good.


00:18:08.044 --> 00:18:11.094
Good. So you are aware
of what might happen


00:18:11.224 --> 00:18:15.320
when untrained personnel enters
without supervision?


00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:16.844
- Don't worry about me.
- Hm?


00:18:23.118 --> 00:18:24.208
Sounds urgent.


00:18:31.135 --> 00:18:32.442
Have they already landed?


00:18:32.572 --> 00:18:35.098
No, they're still in transit.


00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.930
<i>Rubikon to Vesta 2.
What's your request?</i>


00:18:38.061 --> 00:18:39.456
Rubikon, you can hear us?


00:18:39.586 --> 00:18:41.548
<i>W-We're running blind here.</i>


00:18:41.678 --> 00:18:43.942
<i>Can't get contact,
not to ground control</i>


00:18:44.073 --> 00:18:45.728
<i>nor to anyone.</i>


00:18:45.859 --> 00:18:47.099
<i>Is the station
still transmitting our signal?</i>


00:18:47.123 --> 00:18:48.387
Jensen, calm down.


00:18:48.517 --> 00:18:50.739
I'll contact them
and get back to you at once.


00:18:53.353 --> 00:18:56.750
Rubikon to ground control.


00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.276
Ground control, do you read?


00:19:02.763 --> 00:19:04.288
Rubikon to Nibra North.


00:19:10.519 --> 00:19:12.914
Rubikon to Nibvision.


00:19:13.045 --> 00:19:14.919
What's going on?


00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.185
We don't know yet.


00:19:18.316 --> 00:19:19.536
Where are they?


00:19:19.667 --> 00:19:21.279
<i>- Jensen?
- Wagner, yes, tell me.</i>


00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.545
<i>What did... What did they say?</i>


00:19:23.675 --> 00:19:25.767
<i>We can't make contact either.</i>


00:19:25.898 --> 00:19:28.641
<i>- What? Are you kidding me?
- That can't be true.</i>


00:19:28.771 --> 00:19:32.301
We tried all staging posts,
but no one was answering.


00:19:32.432 --> 00:19:34.697
- Jensen, what about Navicon?
- Are you receiving that?


00:19:34.828 --> 00:19:38.835
<i>It stopped just like yours
in the Vesta 1.</i>


00:19:38.966 --> 00:19:42.365
Wait, so they would have
to land without any ground AI?


00:19:42.496 --> 00:19:43.802
A-Are they trained for that?
I...


00:19:43.933 --> 00:19:45.502
I mean,
we weren't trained for that.


00:19:45.632 --> 00:19:47.417
- Don't... Don't worry.
- They...


00:19:47.548 --> 00:19:49.291
T-Their course is
pre-programmed,


00:19:49.421 --> 00:19:50.815
right, Commander?


00:19:50.946 --> 00:19:52.167
- Yes.
- Yes.


00:19:52.298 --> 00:19:54.128
How much time
until they enter orbit?


00:19:54.258 --> 00:19:56.349
54 minutes from now.


00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:59.355
- Okay, Jensen, we're on it.
- We're gonna find a solution


00:19:59.486 --> 00:20:02.492
to get you a connection
to ground. Don't worry, okay?


00:20:02.623 --> 00:20:04.060
<i>Hannah, hurry, please.</i>


00:20:07.982 --> 00:20:10.464
Doctor, send an emergency
signal to all stations,


00:20:10.595 --> 00:20:12.556
even other company stations,
I don't care.


00:20:12.686 --> 00:20:15.780
Gavin, you come with me.


00:20:15.911 --> 00:20:17.435
Maybe they aren't receiving
our signal.


00:20:17.567 --> 00:20:19.438
We have to check
the optical unit.


00:20:22.837 --> 00:20:26.802
.75 bar. Check complete.


00:20:44.316 --> 00:20:45.753
<i>Dad, have you
reached anyone yet?</i>


00:20:45.884 --> 00:20:46.929
Negative.


00:20:48.366 --> 00:20:49.980
<i>We're about to enter atmosphere.</i>


00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:53.115
Uh, good news, uh, I mean,
you are exactly on course.


00:20:53.246 --> 00:20:56.993
<i>Yes, but only if no parameters
change on the way, right?</i>


00:20:57.123 --> 00:21:00.697
- Hold on there. Hold on there.
- You'll be fine.


00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:07.699
<i>Just stay it, Hannah.</i>


00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:10.052
I'm about...


00:22:10.182 --> 00:22:12.144
5 meters away.


00:22:28.089 --> 00:22:29.396
How's she doing?


00:22:29.527 --> 00:22:31.138
Vitals okay.


00:22:31.270 --> 00:22:34.144
Heartbeat slightly increased.
But it's normal.


00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:53.008
Do you get the test signal?


00:22:56.188 --> 00:22:57.758
...Day! May...


00:22:57.889 --> 00:23:00.458
Gavin?


00:23:07.472 --> 00:23:09.737
<i>- Dr. Kry... Jensen?
- Mayday! Mayday!</i>


00:23:09.869 --> 00:23:12.221
<i>- Mayday! To anyone!
- Jensen, what's going on?</i>


00:23:12.352 --> 00:23:14.095
<i>The capsule's heating up
uncontrollably!</i>


00:23:14.225 --> 00:23:15.271
<i>We're gonna burn up!</i>


00:23:15.402 --> 00:23:17.014
Gavin, can you hear that?


00:23:18.538 --> 00:23:20.063
<i>- The shell's about to break!
- Danilo!</i>


00:23:20.194 --> 00:23:21.631
Gavin?


00:23:25.988 --> 00:23:28.471
<i>- Danilo! Danilo!
- Is that you...</i>


00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:32.305
Danilo! Danilo,
what's going on?!


00:23:38.491 --> 00:23:41.323
<i>Gavin?! Gavin, what's
going on down there?!</i>


00:23:41.453 --> 00:23:43.936
<i>Jenson?</i>


00:24:44.886 --> 00:24:46.758
It wasn't our signal.


00:24:46.889 --> 00:24:48.011
Down there, everything is...


00:24:48.066 --> 00:24:50.376
Hannah, but... The crew...


00:24:50.506 --> 00:24:51.595
I know.


00:24:57.563 --> 00:25:00.918
Rubikon to ground control.


00:25:01.048 --> 00:25:02.617
Does anybody hear us?


00:25:07.409 --> 00:25:10.764
Rubikon to ground.


00:25:10.894 --> 00:25:12.375
Anyone.


00:26:22.604 --> 00:26:24.869
<i>Mayday, mayday, mayday!</i>


00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:26.522
<i>- To anyone!
- Jensen, what's going on?</i>


00:26:26.612 --> 00:26:28.214
<i>The capsule is heating up
uncontrollably!</i>


00:26:28.268 --> 00:26:29.444
<i>We're gonna burn up!</i>


00:26:32.449 --> 00:26:34.454
<i>- The shell's about to break!
- Danilo!</i>


00:26:37.459 --> 00:26:40.031
<i>Danilo!</i>


00:26:40.161 --> 00:26:42.295
<i>Danilo!</i>


00:26:42.426 --> 00:26:43.645
<i>Danilo!</i>


00:26:43.776 --> 00:26:44.822
<i>Danilo, what's going on?!</i>


00:26:47.959 --> 00:26:50.966
Sorry, I... I forgot...


00:26:51.096 --> 00:26:53.056
the door.


00:27:02.467 --> 00:27:03.817
It's been two days and...


00:27:03.947 --> 00:27:07.259
I haven't been able
to reach anyone.


00:27:07.391 --> 00:27:11.398
The lasers can't get through
the fog in either direction.


00:27:11.528 --> 00:27:14.229
Could it be the same
as in Ostgrunden?


00:27:14.360 --> 00:27:16.886
Spreading across
the globe that quickly?


00:27:17.017 --> 00:27:19.414
And that would take months,
not days.


00:27:22.245 --> 00:27:24.087
Well, I think we would have
noticed a meteorite


00:27:24.119 --> 00:27:25.600
or a volcano.


00:27:31.002 --> 00:27:34.660
- And what if...
- it was there before,


00:27:34.792 --> 00:27:38.582
in the atmosphere
and just not visible yet.


00:27:38.713 --> 00:27:40.607
You mean the Navicon problem
when we came up here?


00:27:40.631 --> 00:27:42.548
No. I've thought about that,
too,


00:27:42.678 --> 00:27:45.074
but that's why I've been
trying to understand


00:27:45.204 --> 00:27:48.603
this old atmosphere analyzer
thing.


00:27:48.734 --> 00:27:51.958
- And how's that going?
- Really good.


00:27:52.089 --> 00:27:55.965
So far I only found out that
it works without a connection.


00:27:56.096 --> 00:27:59.145
Well, keep trying.


00:28:09.427 --> 00:28:13.217
<i>Dr. Krylow, can I come in?</i>


00:28:20.013 --> 00:28:21.974
I brought you something to eat.


00:28:24.456 --> 00:28:26.461
<i>I know you're hurting, but...</i>


00:28:26.591 --> 00:28:30.120
<i>we need to talk about the algae.</i>


00:28:30.252 --> 00:28:32.518
<i>Our oxy tanks
won't hold forever.</i>


00:28:32.649 --> 00:28:34.521
Go away.


00:28:37.266 --> 00:28:40.053
How far developed
is the gas exchange rate?


00:28:42.189 --> 00:28:44.193
Does the breathing symbiosis
work or not?


00:28:44.323 --> 00:28:46.284
Go away.


00:28:46.414 --> 00:28:48.114
<i>How long can we stay up here?</i>


00:28:50.422 --> 00:28:51.947
<i>- Doctor, please...
- Go away!</i>


00:30:56.198 --> 00:30:57.722
Gavin?


00:30:59.290 --> 00:31:01.731
Gavin, can you come and take
a look at something?


00:31:06.522 --> 00:31:07.916
Gavin!


00:31:31.572 --> 00:31:32.705
Fuck.


00:31:32.835 --> 00:31:34.230
Shit. Shit.


00:31:34.361 --> 00:31:36.452
Doctor!


00:31:38.151 --> 00:31:39.284
Doctor, help me!


00:31:42.116 --> 00:31:44.468
It's an emergency!
Doctor, come!


00:31:48.215 --> 00:31:49.652
Hurry up!


00:31:54.096 --> 00:31:55.490
Doctor! Come on!


00:31:58.018 --> 00:31:59.498
Shit.


00:31:59.628 --> 00:32:00.935
- Hold on.
- He just entered it.


00:32:01.066 --> 00:32:02.592
I'm trying to stop
depressurization.


00:32:02.722 --> 00:32:04.073
Just a second.


00:32:04.203 --> 00:32:05.423
Hm!


00:32:05.553 --> 00:32:06.992
I-It... It has to empty
completely


00:32:07.122 --> 00:32:09.170
before we can fill it up again.


00:32:09.300 --> 00:32:11.042
No, that's... That's too long.


00:32:13.831 --> 00:32:15.312
What are you doing?


00:32:15.443 --> 00:32:16.944
- No, no! No, no, no, no, no!
- I'm trying to bypass


00:32:16.968 --> 00:32:18.426
- the locking mechanism.
- No! No, no, no!


00:32:18.450 --> 00:32:20.322
You will destroy it!


00:32:22.370 --> 00:32:25.552
You can kill us. All of us.
Trust me. Just wait it out.


00:32:25.682 --> 00:32:28.426
Please. Wait it out.


00:32:28.557 --> 00:32:30.474
Come on.


00:32:35.310 --> 00:32:37.270
Come on!


00:32:41.322 --> 00:32:43.064
Empty. Now fast mode.


00:32:43.195 --> 00:32:45.808
Ready?


00:33:00.055 --> 00:33:01.536
Okay, it's open.


00:33:01.666 --> 00:33:03.342
- No, no, no, no, no!
- The pressure is still too much!


00:33:03.366 --> 00:33:05.370
Fucking come on, help me!


00:33:11.687 --> 00:33:12.819
Gavin!


00:33:12.950 --> 00:33:13.995
Gavin!


00:33:14.128 --> 00:33:15.217
Hey.


00:33:15.347 --> 00:33:18.439
Can you hear me?


00:33:18.571 --> 00:33:20.140
- Mouth to mouth.
- Come on.


00:33:29.636 --> 00:33:31.859
5, 4, 3, 2, 1.


00:33:39.220 --> 00:33:41.704
5, 4, 3, 2, 1.


00:33:46.495 --> 00:33:48.195
Okay, again.


00:33:55.557 --> 00:33:57.865
Okay.


00:33:57.996 --> 00:33:59.261
Be careful.


00:34:17.689 --> 00:34:19.693
Okay, that's not ripped.


00:34:19.823 --> 00:34:22.046
Is he, um...


00:34:22.176 --> 00:34:24.355
Is he going to be okay?


00:34:24.485 --> 00:34:26.881
Eh, I don't know. I hope so.


00:34:30.845 --> 00:34:32.720
Why the hell would he do that?


00:34:32.850 --> 00:34:35.420
- Hm?
- Why would he do that?


00:34:35.551 --> 00:34:37.423
Ah, I don't know.


00:34:37.555 --> 00:34:40.561
And frankly, I don't care.


00:34:40.691 --> 00:34:42.346
What's wrong with you? He...


00:34:42.478 --> 00:34:44.918
He just tried to kill himsef
and you don't care?


00:34:45.048 --> 00:34:47.793
Excuse me?


00:34:47.923 --> 00:34:49.623
You know what? You do it.


00:34:53.718 --> 00:34:56.115
What? They didn't
teach you that


00:34:56.245 --> 00:34:58.032
at Spy Academy?


00:35:04.043 --> 00:35:05.307
Oh, yeah, I know.


00:35:05.438 --> 00:35:08.357
Know what?


00:35:08.487 --> 00:35:10.208
That your algae system
is much more advanced


00:35:10.272 --> 00:35:12.495
than you want to admit?
Oh, that's a big surprise.


00:35:12.626 --> 00:35:14.193
Oh, you think I'm an idiot?


00:35:14.324 --> 00:35:15.433
I'm going to tell anything
to the Nibra spy?


00:35:15.457 --> 00:35:18.028
- No.
- It's not spying.


00:35:18.159 --> 00:35:19.726
They funded it.
It belongs to them.


00:35:19.856 --> 00:35:22.689
No, it doesn't!


00:35:22.820 --> 00:35:26.000
It doesn't belong to them.


00:35:26.130 --> 00:35:28.179
It belongs to me...


00:35:28.309 --> 00:35:30.052
and it belongs to Danilo.


00:35:36.456 --> 00:35:38.373
I'm sorry about your son.


00:35:42.512 --> 00:35:44.995
Come on, you must be tired.
Just go to bed.


00:35:45.126 --> 00:35:46.608
I can take care of him.


00:36:38.188 --> 00:36:40.934
Gavin?


00:36:41.065 --> 00:36:43.417
I closed my eyes for one second.


00:36:55.353 --> 00:36:57.532
Hey, Gavin.


00:36:57.663 --> 00:36:59.100
Gavin, h-how do you feel?


00:37:13.216 --> 00:37:15.090
- Let me check you here...
- Get off me!


00:37:15.221 --> 00:37:17.485
I... I'm sorry, I...


00:37:17.616 --> 00:37:18.880
I...


00:37:19.010 --> 00:37:20.579
Calm down.


00:37:20.710 --> 00:37:22.060
You don't understand.


00:37:22.190 --> 00:37:23.977
- You need to lay down.
- This fog is toxic.


00:37:24.107 --> 00:37:26.722
- Okay?
- These aerosols, they...


00:37:26.851 --> 00:37:28.420
- Calm down.
- They're all dead.


00:37:28.550 --> 00:37:30.947
- Okay.
- They're all dead.


00:37:31.078 --> 00:37:34.432
Nobody can survive this
in that... Dimitri...


00:37:34.562 --> 00:37:37.308
- They're all dead.
- Hey. Hey.


00:37:37.438 --> 00:37:39.660
Breathe, breathe deeply.


00:37:39.790 --> 00:37:41.969
I can't breathe.


00:37:42.100 --> 00:37:44.670
Everyone down there...


00:38:15.123 --> 00:38:18.521
Family? Friends?


00:38:18.651 --> 00:38:20.917
You have someone out there?


00:38:23.182 --> 00:38:24.925
My little sister.


00:38:28.149 --> 00:38:29.848
Sorry.


00:38:33.115 --> 00:38:34.771
But it doesn't matter.


00:38:34.901 --> 00:38:37.037
We'll suffocate up here anyway.


00:38:42.352 --> 00:38:44.051
We're safe here.


00:38:49.279 --> 00:38:50.979
Okay?


00:38:51.109 --> 00:38:53.111
Danilo and I...


00:38:53.243 --> 00:38:56.772
achieved a working symbiosis
with the algae.


00:38:56.903 --> 00:38:58.776
We can survive.


00:39:01.869 --> 00:39:04.614
Thank you...


00:39:04.744 --> 00:39:06.792
for telling a Nibra spy.


00:39:08.883 --> 00:39:10.626
You're welcome.


00:39:13.413 --> 00:39:14.981
Where you going?


00:39:19.469 --> 00:39:22.780
Wow. You've been busy.


00:39:22.911 --> 00:39:26.221
<i>Even if the air is toxic,
there are bunkers.</i>


00:39:26.352 --> 00:39:30.797
The lasers can't get through
the fog, but maybe this can.


00:39:30.928 --> 00:39:33.194
I'm trying to get it to work.


00:39:33.325 --> 00:39:35.632
- Good.
- Is this...


00:39:35.763 --> 00:39:39.554
The old ISS radio system,
exactly.


00:39:39.685 --> 00:39:41.557
That's ancient technology.


00:39:41.688 --> 00:39:44.434
I mean, do you really think
anyone is still using it?


00:39:46.131 --> 00:39:48.048
I'll find out.


00:39:48.179 --> 00:39:51.534
I just need
to reactivate the radio antenna.


00:39:51.664 --> 00:39:56.370
Radio antenna? But...
No, you can't do that alone.


00:39:56.500 --> 00:39:58.591
Yeah, I know.


00:39:58.722 --> 00:40:00.160
Take a seat.


00:40:05.736 --> 00:40:09.177
<i>Look for a circuit in
sector... Sector B.</i>


00:40:11.879 --> 00:40:14.145
<i>Can you see it?</i>


00:40:14.276 --> 00:40:15.844
The cables are tangled.


00:40:18.241 --> 00:40:21.115
<i>Okay, wait. I got it.</i>


00:40:21.246 --> 00:40:22.685
Affirmative.


00:40:22.815 --> 00:40:25.690
Okay. So redirect it.


00:40:27.084 --> 00:40:30.003
I keep seeing
all this useless crap here.


00:40:30.133 --> 00:40:32.965
Yeah. I've lived on
this station for 8 years.


00:40:33.096 --> 00:40:35.014
I've seen it all.


00:40:35.144 --> 00:40:36.973
That's what happens
when it's too expensive


00:40:37.105 --> 00:40:38.497
to get rid of old parts.


00:40:38.628 --> 00:40:41.635
Just pair them up together.


00:40:41.765 --> 00:40:43.813
Your domer friend was right.


00:40:43.943 --> 00:40:46.384
This station is a junkyard.


00:40:53.310 --> 00:40:56.273
Yeah. Tell me about it.


00:40:56.404 --> 00:41:01.893
<i>When I was young,
astronauts were like gods.</i>


00:41:02.024 --> 00:41:06.728
Well, when you were young,
countries existed still.


00:41:06.861 --> 00:41:10.910
<i>- Okay, Doctor, it's attached.
- Wait.</i>


00:41:11.041 --> 00:41:13.002
Very good. And by the way,


00:41:13.133 --> 00:41:16.313
you don't have to
call me doctor all the time.


00:41:16.444 --> 00:41:18.536
<i>My real name is Dimitri.</i>


00:41:20.408 --> 00:41:24.416
I think I'm getting
a signal here...


00:41:24.548 --> 00:41:25.811
<i>Dimitri.</i>


00:41:28.859 --> 00:41:31.169
- Give me a second.
- Let me scan it.


00:41:34.480 --> 00:41:36.223
Got it.


00:41:36.353 --> 00:41:38.009
Okay.


00:41:45.414 --> 00:41:47.027
Let's give it a try.


00:41:53.082 --> 00:41:54.869
Commander Wagner to ground.


00:42:01.448 --> 00:42:03.059
Can anybody hear me?


00:42:07.938 --> 00:42:09.551
Please, anyone?


00:42:14.691 --> 00:42:16.128
Hello?


00:42:17.523 --> 00:42:19.134
Fuck!


00:42:26.498 --> 00:42:28.065
Gavin can't be right.


00:42:30.985 --> 00:42:32.771
They can't be dead.


00:42:44.535 --> 00:42:47.322
Open the door!


00:42:47.454 --> 00:42:48.760
Come on!


00:43:09.235 --> 00:43:10.630
Your ears hut?


00:43:10.761 --> 00:43:12.765
I, uh... I can give you
some painkillers


00:43:12.895 --> 00:43:14.776
- for the... for the ears.
- I'm fine. I'm fine.


00:43:14.812 --> 00:43:16.338
Are you sure?


00:43:19.211 --> 00:43:22.044
So there's no doubt
about what you said?


00:43:27.142 --> 00:43:32.370
The chemical structure of the
fog's aerosols is highly toxic.


00:43:32.500 --> 00:43:33.982
It's lethal.


00:43:34.112 --> 00:43:36.160
Where did it come from?


00:43:36.290 --> 00:43:37.815
I don't know. I...


00:43:37.945 --> 00:43:40.864
To me, it seems like
some kind of... chain reaction.


00:43:40.995 --> 00:43:42.869
From what?


00:43:43.000 --> 00:43:45.091
Permafrost gases.


00:43:45.221 --> 00:43:48.271
We've been warning people
about this for years,


00:43:48.402 --> 00:43:51.145
and now, they've obviously
reacted with something,


00:43:51.276 --> 00:43:53.716
like maybe toxins
from the power plants,


00:43:53.848 --> 00:43:56.505
some other pollution,
maybe chemical weapons


00:43:56.635 --> 00:43:58.247
from another corporation war.


00:43:58.378 --> 00:44:00.513
Fact is, it's...
It's all over down there.


00:44:00.643 --> 00:44:02.254
We fucked it.


00:44:02.385 --> 00:44:05.044
Apparently, the economy was
more important than breathing.


00:44:05.174 --> 00:44:06.742
And what about the air domes?


00:44:06.874 --> 00:44:09.444
They're for a very specific
molecular spectrum.


00:44:09.574 --> 00:44:11.449
Only a closed system
with oxygen tanks


00:44:11.579 --> 00:44:12.775
could shield them from the fog.


00:44:12.799 --> 00:44:14.366
But there are bunkers like that.


00:44:14.497 --> 00:44:16.895
The evacuation bunkers.
I trained in them.


00:44:17.025 --> 00:44:19.595
And what will happen
to the people in there, hm?


00:44:19.726 --> 00:44:21.327
Sooner or later,
they'll run out of food.


00:44:21.380 --> 00:44:22.862
They'll run out of oxygen.


00:44:22.993 --> 00:44:25.432
Same as us.
We're all just living corpses.


00:44:25.563 --> 00:44:26.584
- Gavin...
- And I don't like the idea


00:44:26.608 --> 00:44:28.051
- of a slow death.
- We can stay here


00:44:28.134 --> 00:44:29.920
as long as we need to.


00:44:33.143 --> 00:44:35.452
The algae-gas exchange works.


00:44:42.073 --> 00:44:43.206
No.


00:44:43.337 --> 00:44:44.732
What?


00:44:44.863 --> 00:44:46.736
No.


00:44:46.867 --> 00:44:49.349
I-I...
I can't live like this,


00:44:49.481 --> 00:44:52.878
stuck in this...
In this tiny metal can forever.


00:44:53.008 --> 00:44:56.539
- Maybe you two can.
- I-I... I just can't.


00:44:56.670 --> 00:45:00.722
Yeah, and w-what
is the alternative?


00:45:00.852 --> 00:45:02.638
Will you try it again?


00:45:06.297 --> 00:45:09.914
Look, it's your life.
Your decision.


00:45:10.044 --> 00:45:12.746
I just want you to know
that if you try it again,


00:45:12.876 --> 00:45:14.444
it will also kill her.


00:45:17.057 --> 00:45:18.758
Then me.


00:45:18.888 --> 00:45:21.719
What? Why?


00:45:21.850 --> 00:45:23.202
I didn't tell you this yet,


00:45:23.332 --> 00:45:25.945
but the system is designed
for a full crew of six.


00:45:26.075 --> 00:45:30.825
They produce CO2 and the system
converts it back into oxygen.


00:45:33.962 --> 00:45:37.708
The bare minimum for
an efficient gas exchange


00:45:37.838 --> 00:45:40.278
is three people.


00:45:40.409 --> 00:45:43.503
Gavin, I need your CO2.


00:46:23.277 --> 00:46:24.978
Can I join?


00:46:28.374 --> 00:46:30.074
Okay.


00:46:38.569 --> 00:46:41.227
I'm mad at you, you know.


00:46:41.358 --> 00:46:46.282
For leaving me alone here
with this old grumpy cat.


00:46:55.866 --> 00:46:57.783
What?


00:46:57.913 --> 00:47:00.526
What?
What's so funny?


00:47:00.657 --> 00:47:02.967
It's... It's just that I...


00:47:03.097 --> 00:47:05.449
I worked my ass off,


00:47:05.580 --> 00:47:08.368
Debit Point for Debit Point,


00:47:08.500 --> 00:47:11.505
one shitty mission
after another,


00:47:11.635 --> 00:47:15.775
and for what?
For this?


00:47:17.910 --> 00:47:20.176
I could have partied more,


00:47:20.306 --> 00:47:25.142
like Knopf or taking a day off
every once in a while.


00:47:28.235 --> 00:47:31.328
Yeah.


00:47:31.459 --> 00:47:36.556
I think I've really screwed up
this whole life thing.


00:47:42.175 --> 00:47:44.049
Same here.


00:47:44.179 --> 00:47:47.578
You think I was not screwing up
my life by going on protests


00:47:47.708 --> 00:47:50.497
and not washing
and cutting out T-shirts and...


00:47:50.627 --> 00:47:52.326
I'm really glad I did that,
now, aren't I?


00:47:54.286 --> 00:47:57.205
- Yeah.
- "And there's no Planet B."


00:48:00.517 --> 00:48:02.173
And Dimitri...


00:48:02.303 --> 00:48:04.656
don't think he was partying
in... in his lab


00:48:04.787 --> 00:48:07.574
with his working symbiosis.


00:48:14.414 --> 00:48:15.856
Can you imagine if they knew
on earth


00:48:15.896 --> 00:48:17.246
that we were the last 3 humans?


00:48:17.377 --> 00:48:19.729
- Oh, my God.
- A bunch of losers


00:48:19.860 --> 00:48:21.081
and freaks.


00:48:30.359 --> 00:48:34.063
Me and my friends fought so hard


00:48:34.193 --> 00:48:37.329
for a planet
that doesn't exist anymore.


00:48:40.684 --> 00:48:44.258
We spent so long believing
in something.


00:48:44.388 --> 00:48:47.654
Now it doesn't mean anything.


00:48:50.051 --> 00:48:53.885
So the naive activist is gone?


00:48:55.019 --> 00:48:56.499
Hmm.


00:48:59.592 --> 00:49:01.466
He was kind of an idiot anyway.


00:49:03.731 --> 00:49:06.476
That's too bad.


00:49:06.606 --> 00:49:08.087
I liked him.


00:49:52.612 --> 00:49:54.006
Dimitri?


00:49:58.668 --> 00:50:00.060
What?


00:50:00.191 --> 00:50:01.368
Is that normal?


00:50:06.510 --> 00:50:10.473
Eh, they never keep
the exact same green color.


00:50:10.604 --> 00:50:11.780
How much longer?


00:50:11.910 --> 00:50:14.002
I'm dying. This time for real.


00:50:14.133 --> 00:50:15.396
Two more minutes.


00:50:16.790 --> 00:50:20.972
- Yeah, but... But brown?
- That's... That's weird.


00:50:21.102 --> 00:50:24.327
It can happen if, uh...


00:50:24.458 --> 00:50:26.332
No, don't worry. It's fine.


00:50:28.816 --> 00:50:30.688
No, no. No. No.


00:50:31.821 --> 00:50:33.520
That's it, I'm done.


00:50:33.651 --> 00:50:35.917
You'll have to wait
for my breath until tomorrow.


00:50:36.047 --> 00:50:39.271
Gavin, that wasn't 45 minutes.


00:50:39.402 --> 00:50:41.144
Do you even know
how long that is?


00:50:41.276 --> 00:50:42.471
No, of course you don't, because
he's always


00:50:42.495 --> 00:50:44.237
hammering me, pedaling.


00:50:44.367 --> 00:50:46.690
Actually, I do know because
every morning when you cuddle,


00:50:46.808 --> 00:50:49.160
I pedal, at least 45 minutes.


00:50:49.291 --> 00:50:50.947
Maybe we should check that
on the CCTV.


00:50:51.077 --> 00:50:53.211
- Maybe we should.
- Okay. Okay.


00:50:53.342 --> 00:50:54.867
What do you say?


00:50:54.997 --> 00:50:56.086
Movie night?


00:50:56.217 --> 00:50:58.614
- Sure.
- What else?


00:51:09.157 --> 00:51:11.857
Dimitri?


00:51:11.988 --> 00:51:14.603
- Yeah. Choose something.
- I'm, uh...


00:51:14.734 --> 00:51:16.258
I'll come in a second.


00:51:42.442 --> 00:51:44.315
Sorry, guys. Sorry.


00:51:44.446 --> 00:51:47.539
Oh, you waited for me.
That's nice.


00:51:47.669 --> 00:51:48.845
Where have you been?


00:51:48.976 --> 00:51:51.850
I'm just, uh...
What are we watching?


00:51:51.982 --> 00:51:54.466
Nothing if you can't
reactivate the internet.


00:51:54.596 --> 00:51:58.604
Apparently we've reached the end
of the internal movie library.


00:51:58.735 --> 00:52:00.391
Oh.


00:52:07.883 --> 00:52:09.584
I can offer you a drink.


00:52:10.890 --> 00:52:12.327
More! More! More!


00:52:12.458 --> 00:52:15.378
- More! More! More!
- Hannushka, that's enough.


00:52:15.509 --> 00:52:17.032
You had enough, Hannushka.


00:52:17.162 --> 00:52:19.036
Yeah. Thank you, Daddy.


00:52:19.166 --> 00:52:20.780
Okay.


00:52:20.910 --> 00:52:23.393
Of all your algae's functions,
this is definitely my favorite.


00:52:23.524 --> 00:52:26.487
Yeah, well, this batch is
a bit too strong.


00:52:26.618 --> 00:52:28.271
- You can see that.
- If I had known


00:52:28.403 --> 00:52:30.362
you had a whole distillery
hidden in your lab,


00:52:30.493 --> 00:52:32.039
I would have just...
Yeah, you would just


00:52:32.063 --> 00:52:34.284
report me to Nibra,
wouldn't you, little spy?


00:52:34.415 --> 00:52:38.074
Yes, probably.


00:52:38.204 --> 00:52:39.425
Wait, what?


00:52:39.556 --> 00:52:41.254
What, you didn't know?


00:52:41.384 --> 00:52:43.781
Hannushka was sent by Nibra


00:52:43.913 --> 00:52:46.308
- to steal my mother cultures.
- What the fuck?


00:52:46.439 --> 00:52:47.791
It's not... No, not stealing.


00:52:47.922 --> 00:52:49.443
- Not stealing.
- Steal is a hard word.


00:52:49.490 --> 00:52:51.164
- Just taking away.
- Steal. Take away and steal.


00:52:51.188 --> 00:52:52.277
- No.
- What?


00:52:52.407 --> 00:52:53.890
- No.
- Five weeks


00:52:54.021 --> 00:52:55.632
and you're only mentioning
this... now?


00:52:55.763 --> 00:52:57.810
I am so sorry, my dear.


00:52:59.597 --> 00:53:01.688
Hey.


00:53:01.818 --> 00:53:04.432
Y-You were hiding the samples?


00:53:04.563 --> 00:53:07.221
I was helping.


00:53:07.351 --> 00:53:10.575
Three months ago, Nibra
changed their contract.


00:53:10.706 --> 00:53:12.840
Suddenly they wanted the...
The system


00:53:12.971 --> 00:53:15.672
to be exclusive
for their air domes.


00:53:15.803 --> 00:53:18.591
And I-I wouldn't mind.
I would have taken the money,


00:53:18.722 --> 00:53:22.947
- which was a lot of money.
- Gree-dy fuck.


00:53:23.078 --> 00:53:26.040
Uh, yeah, and not ashamed of it.


00:53:26.171 --> 00:53:30.397
But then, Danilo, no.
He was furious.


00:53:30.528 --> 00:53:33.098
He decided to make it
a public domain.


00:53:33.228 --> 00:53:37.498
He found some secret...
Eh, I don't know, distributor.


00:53:37.629 --> 00:53:41.768
Huh. Actually sounds like
a good guy.


00:53:41.898 --> 00:53:44.557
Extremely annoying.


00:53:44.688 --> 00:53:45.994
Stubborn.


00:53:46.125 --> 00:53:47.736
Rude.


00:53:47.868 --> 00:53:49.219
A little bit like you.


00:53:50.961 --> 00:53:55.056
Cheeky little do-gooder shit,
huh?


00:53:56.449 --> 00:53:57.975
Sorry.


00:54:00.545 --> 00:54:02.940
- Thank you.
- No, you...


00:54:03.071 --> 00:54:04.421
Okay. Okay.


00:54:04.552 --> 00:54:06.949
Show me what you got, boys.


00:54:07.080 --> 00:54:08.953
Uh... Yeah, this is garbage.


00:54:09.084 --> 00:54:11.350
- No!
- No, you are done.


00:54:11.480 --> 00:54:12.787
- What the...?
- Boom!


00:54:12.918 --> 00:54:13.658
No! Gavin!


00:54:13.788 --> 00:54:15.749
- Ooh!
- Fuck off!


00:54:15.879 --> 00:54:17.622
- Ooh!
- No, I'm... Okay...


00:54:17.754 --> 00:54:19.147
Stop it.


00:54:19.278 --> 00:54:23.505
No. And you two should be
so fucking ashamed,


00:54:23.636 --> 00:54:25.029
bleeding out the poor.


00:54:27.730 --> 00:54:29.473
I need to dance...


00:54:29.603 --> 00:54:33.438
- or I'll die.
- Oh, no.


00:54:43.457 --> 00:54:45.331
Gavin...


00:54:45.461 --> 00:54:47.203
dance with the woman.


00:54:47.334 --> 00:54:48.510
Come on, dance.


00:54:48.641 --> 00:54:50.035
- Please.
- Come on.


00:54:50.167 --> 00:54:51.691
Gavin. Oh, sorry.


00:54:51.822 --> 00:54:53.347
- No, please.
- Let's go.


00:54:53.477 --> 00:54:55.219
Come on! Come on.


00:54:55.351 --> 00:54:56.701
Move the hips. Hips.


00:54:56.832 --> 00:54:58.836
I'm moving... Ow!


00:54:58.966 --> 00:55:01.188
I think you should get Dimitri
to dance.


00:55:02.408 --> 00:55:04.325
- Old guy to dance!
- No, no, no!


00:55:04.456 --> 00:55:05.763
- Come on!
- No!


00:55:05.893 --> 00:55:07.438
Please, no! I'm a scientist!
I'm not a dancer!


00:55:07.462 --> 00:55:08.900
- Yes, you are.
- I'm not a dancer.


00:55:09.031 --> 00:55:10.226
- Come on!
- You are definitely drunk enough


00:55:10.250 --> 00:55:11.426
- to dance.
- Come on!


00:55:11.557 --> 00:55:15.435
Come on, Dimitri. Yeah.


00:55:15.566 --> 00:55:17.830
Come on!


00:56:36.249 --> 00:56:39.168
<i>If anyone else is out there,
please answer.</i>


00:56:39.299 --> 00:56:41.128
<i>We're a group of survivors
in a bunker</i>


00:56:41.258 --> 00:56:43.089
<i>underneath Nibra Headquarters.</i>


00:56:43.220 --> 00:56:46.530
<i>If you can hear us,
please respond.</i>


00:56:46.661 --> 00:56:49.102
Gavin! Gavin!


00:56:49.233 --> 00:56:51.062
Hey, you guys, wake up!


00:56:53.283 --> 00:56:57.552
- Hey, Gavin!
- Gavin, wake up. Come on.


00:56:57.683 --> 00:56:58.792
The laser comm worked again.


00:56:58.816 --> 00:57:00.777
I-I talked to one
of the survivors!


00:57:00.907 --> 00:57:01.997
Wh... O-Oh...


00:57:02.127 --> 00:57:04.044
Come on! Come on!


00:57:04.175 --> 00:57:05.787
Dimitri!


00:57:05.917 --> 00:57:07.224
Hey! They're alive!


00:57:07.355 --> 00:57:08.748
There are survivors down there.


00:57:08.879 --> 00:57:10.710
Oh, good. Right.


00:57:17.157 --> 00:57:20.076
- Rubikon to survivors.
- Can you hear us?


00:57:23.605 --> 00:57:25.826
<i>- Hello? Commander Wagner?
- Is this thing working?</i>


00:57:28.005 --> 00:57:29.835
<i>- Yes. Yes, it is.
- Oh, my God.</i>


00:57:29.966 --> 00:57:31.883
And we're happy
to hear your voice.


00:57:32.014 --> 00:57:36.195
<i>- Uh, this Esther Chen-Kaminski.
- I'm our representative.</i>


00:57:36.326 --> 00:57:38.854
How many of you are there?


00:57:38.984 --> 00:57:40.945
<i>We're almost 300 here.</i>


00:57:43.168 --> 00:57:44.735
<i>Was there an attack?</i>


00:57:44.866 --> 00:57:48.307
<i>- Honestly, we don't know.
- The fog came so suddenly</i>


00:57:48.438 --> 00:57:51.531
<i>and people started
coughing and dropping.</i>


00:57:51.661 --> 00:57:53.317
<i>It was...</i>


00:57:53.448 --> 00:57:56.017
<i>But the soldiers
brought us into the bunker.</i>


00:57:56.148 --> 00:57:57.804
But you're safe, aren't you?


00:57:59.852 --> 00:58:02.161
<i>No. It's the oxygen.</i>


00:58:02.292 --> 00:58:06.212
<i>We don't have much left, but
I guess Krylow's algae system</i>


00:58:06.343 --> 00:58:08.172
<i>is preventing that for you,
right?</i>


00:58:11.440 --> 00:58:14.142
How do you know about the algae?


00:58:14.272 --> 00:58:17.932
<i>Well, some of us own stock
in this promising project.</i>


00:58:18.062 --> 00:58:21.286
So you're CEOs or something.


00:58:21.417 --> 00:58:24.728
<i>And their families, yes.</i>


00:58:24.859 --> 00:58:29.476
I-Is there a Randall Abbott
amongst you?


00:58:29.608 --> 00:58:31.480
<i>I'm sorry. No.</i>


00:58:35.794 --> 00:58:38.930
<i>But... So these algae, uh...</i>


00:58:39.061 --> 00:58:40.804
<i>The system provides for you,
right?</i>


00:58:40.934 --> 00:58:43.548
<i>I mean, Dr. Krylow
made that work?</i>


00:59:51.904 --> 00:59:53.210
Dimitri.


00:59:53.341 --> 00:59:55.998
- Hmm?
- He's in here.


00:59:56.130 --> 01:00:00.486
Hannah was right.
There are survivors. Almost 300.


01:00:00.617 --> 01:00:02.011
- Really?
- Yeah.


01:00:02.142 --> 01:00:06.149
But even better, there are
these openings in the fog.


01:00:06.279 --> 01:00:08.415
Very small ones, but still.


01:00:10.550 --> 01:00:13.382
- Hmm.
- That's why they could hear us.


01:00:13.512 --> 01:00:15.036
They've already managed
to transfer


01:00:15.167 --> 01:00:17.084
their bunkers' coordinates.


01:00:17.214 --> 01:00:18.609
The next step would be
the Vesta.


01:00:18.740 --> 01:00:20.874
With Gavin's atmosphere
analysis,


01:00:21.005 --> 01:00:23.009
I might manage
to fly down manually.


01:00:23.139 --> 01:00:24.403
To do what?


01:00:24.534 --> 01:00:25.643
Their bunker provides
enough oxygen


01:00:25.667 --> 01:00:27.801
- for three more weeks, at best.
- Mm-hmm.


01:00:27.932 --> 01:00:29.675
If...


01:00:31.461 --> 01:00:34.771
If we could bring your algae
down there, we could help them.


01:00:37.996 --> 01:00:39.390
- Okay.
- Look, they're supposed


01:00:39.521 --> 01:00:41.090
to nourish a closed system.


01:00:41.221 --> 01:00:43.093
It doesn't matter
if it's a bunker down there


01:00:43.225 --> 01:00:44.986
- or the Rubikon up here.
- Hold on one second.


01:00:45.010 --> 01:00:49.846
So are you suggesting we fly
down without Navicon?


01:00:49.977 --> 01:00:52.809
Yes.


01:00:54.072 --> 01:00:57.558
We could save 300 lives.


01:00:57.688 --> 01:00:59.256
Look, we think it's
a risk worth taking.


01:00:59.386 --> 01:01:01.565
Let's say we...
We make it to earth.


01:01:01.695 --> 01:01:03.483
How do we get to the bunkers?


01:01:03.613 --> 01:01:05.593
- They have mobile oxy tanks.
- They could pick us up.


01:01:05.617 --> 01:01:07.490
Also the equipment
from the Nibra lab.


01:01:07.620 --> 01:01:10.017
It's pretty close
to where we'd land.


01:01:10.147 --> 01:01:14.853
Oh. Oh, it seems like
you've figured it all out.


01:01:14.983 --> 01:01:20.778
Great.
S-So w-what if I say no?


01:01:20.908 --> 01:01:23.565
What? W-Why?


01:01:23.696 --> 01:01:27.661
B-Because, you know,
i-i-it's a little irresponsible


01:01:27.792 --> 01:01:30.886
and very, very stupid.


01:01:31.016 --> 01:01:33.586
Flying down without Navicon?
Are you out of your minds?


01:01:33.717 --> 01:01:35.038
So, what? We do...
We do nothing?


01:01:35.155 --> 01:01:36.680
We just watch them die?


01:01:36.811 --> 01:01:38.422
Are you really that selfish?


01:01:38.553 --> 01:01:39.879
C-Can you stop with
the Green Fighter bullshit?


01:01:39.903 --> 01:01:41.908
It's not one of your
awareness projects.


01:01:42.038 --> 01:01:44.565
- We have to help if we ca.
- We have a moral responsibility.


01:01:44.695 --> 01:01:48.137
My only moral responsibility
is to keep you and you alive.


01:01:48.268 --> 01:01:49.942
- That's it.
- Isn't this what Danilo would


01:01:49.966 --> 01:01:51.490
have wanted... to help people?


01:01:51.621 --> 01:01:53.713
Yes, he did.


01:01:53.844 --> 01:01:56.589
And now he's dead.


01:01:56.719 --> 01:02:01.336
But I'm here, and I say
tough luck to them.


01:02:01.467 --> 01:02:03.907
I know now
how to make mother cultures.


01:02:04.039 --> 01:02:06.696
So we don't need your help.


01:02:06.826 --> 01:02:08.107
You're not going to touch them.


01:02:08.220 --> 01:02:09.548
- Hey.
- You understand what I'm saying?


01:02:09.572 --> 01:02:11.028
<i>- You're not going to touch it!
- Stop!</i>


01:02:11.052 --> 01:02:13.753
Seriously, you guys.


01:02:13.885 --> 01:02:16.064
Sit down, both of you.


01:02:28.436 --> 01:02:31.441
We have to make a decision.


01:02:31.571 --> 01:02:33.751
I-I-It really doesn't
make sense.


01:02:33.881 --> 01:02:36.930
Come on. W-We are fine.
We are good here.


01:02:37.061 --> 01:02:40.241
We... We can stay here
as long as we want.


01:02:40.373 --> 01:02:43.378
- Really?
- That's your plan?


01:02:43.508 --> 01:02:46.340
Have you gone completely crazy
in that lab all this time?


01:02:46.471 --> 01:02:49.434
You don't get to talk to me
about crazy, mister.


01:02:49.565 --> 01:02:51.525
I am not the one
who tried to kill himself.


01:02:51.656 --> 01:02:53.964
How desperately are you trying
to do it again?


01:02:54.095 --> 01:02:56.273
- Really?
- You're going to go there?


01:02:56.404 --> 01:02:58.235
Hey, I'm not done
talking to you.


01:02:58.365 --> 01:03:00.152
Hey. Hey, come back.
Come...


01:03:00.283 --> 01:03:02.025
Danilo!


01:03:15.311 --> 01:03:17.534
You okay?


01:03:17.664 --> 01:03:19.190
Nothing. It's...


01:03:23.547 --> 01:03:25.811
Hey. Hey. Hey. You okay?


01:03:25.942 --> 01:03:29.950
- It's nothing.
- It's just...


01:03:30.081 --> 01:03:32.259
It's just your schnapps,
I guess.


01:03:42.017 --> 01:03:43.934
- What are you doing?
- Just a precaution.


01:03:44.065 --> 01:03:47.246
Just want to make sure
everything is fine.


01:03:47.376 --> 01:03:49.992
Thank you.


01:03:50.122 --> 01:03:51.864
He's right, you know.


01:03:51.995 --> 01:03:54.696
What if those are the last
people on the planet?


01:03:58.007 --> 01:04:01.928
Well, if these are
the last people on the planet,


01:04:02.059 --> 01:04:05.936
maybe it's not
that bit of an idea


01:04:06.066 --> 01:04:08.331
to start it all from scratch.


01:04:08.462 --> 01:04:11.294
Dimitri, come on.


01:04:11.424 --> 01:04:14.301
Okay, tell me.


01:04:14.431 --> 01:04:19.223
What have these people,
these lovely CEOs,


01:04:19.353 --> 01:04:22.011
ever done for you?


01:04:22.142 --> 01:04:26.325
- They got me out of the Third.
- Hmm.


01:04:26.455 --> 01:04:32.075
Yeah. And made you a soldier
to save them in the army.


01:04:32.206 --> 01:04:34.777
You done?


01:04:51.898 --> 01:04:53.946
Can't sleep?


01:04:59.043 --> 01:05:02.092
Is that her? Knopf?


01:05:02.223 --> 01:05:03.966
Her real name is Mia.


01:05:05.925 --> 01:05:08.976
This was the last message
I got from her.


01:05:09.106 --> 01:05:12.721
I'm trying to find out
where she was.


01:05:12.852 --> 01:05:14.899
Okay.


01:05:15.031 --> 01:05:16.425
Knopf was stationed 5 hours away


01:05:16.555 --> 01:05:18.559
from the Nibra central bunker.


01:05:18.691 --> 01:05:20.105
There are other bunkers
in that area,


01:05:20.129 --> 01:05:25.139
and she got
an evacuation order, too.


01:05:25.270 --> 01:05:27.491
That means
she could still be alive.


01:05:30.106 --> 01:05:32.283
Why didn't you tell me?


01:05:32.413 --> 01:05:33.982
Because it's...


01:05:34.113 --> 01:05:37.163
It's stupid.


01:05:37.294 --> 01:05:38.992
It's such a small chance.


01:06:16.763 --> 01:06:19.073
We are preparing for departure.


01:06:19.204 --> 01:06:21.164
Will you help us load
the mother cultures?


01:06:27.394 --> 01:06:29.137
Dimitri...


01:06:29.267 --> 01:06:31.446
Either you come with us or...


01:06:31.577 --> 01:06:33.275
Or you stay.


01:06:41.857 --> 01:06:43.992
What?! In here as well?


01:06:44.123 --> 01:06:46.170
- No, no.
- Don't say we're losing them now.


01:06:46.300 --> 01:06:49.264
I-Is this a trick
to make us stay?


01:06:49.394 --> 01:06:54.188
- No, it's not a trick.
- It's really happening


01:06:54.318 --> 01:06:56.321
in the whole station.


01:06:56.452 --> 01:06:58.064
Are they sick?


01:06:58.195 --> 01:06:59.763
That's what I thought.


01:06:59.895 --> 01:07:02.160
- So what?
- We can't bring them down? Or...


01:07:02.291 --> 01:07:03.467
Dimitri...


01:07:05.428 --> 01:07:08.215
- It's you.
- I make them go...


01:07:08.345 --> 01:07:10.307
I don't even touch them
without your supervision.


01:07:10.437 --> 01:07:12.180
You don't need to touch them.


01:07:12.311 --> 01:07:16.581
They feed from our urine
in the station's nutrient cycle.


01:07:16.711 --> 01:07:20.849
So they've changed color
because of Hannah's pee?


01:07:20.979 --> 01:07:22.722
Exactly.


01:07:25.598 --> 01:07:29.780
- Yeah. Yeah.
- You almost got me. Come on.


01:07:29.910 --> 01:07:34.005
The algae is extremely
sensitive to hormones.


01:07:34.137 --> 01:07:36.053
It's your high levels of HCG
that did it.


01:07:36.183 --> 01:07:38.624
No, soldiers can't get pregnant.


01:07:38.754 --> 01:07:40.104
W-We don't even get our periods.


01:07:40.235 --> 01:07:43.024
I'm... I'm sterile
till the end of my duty.


01:07:43.155 --> 01:07:45.943
Unless your hormone inducer
loses connection


01:07:46.074 --> 01:07:48.514
with its control unit for
a long enough time.


01:07:59.274 --> 01:08:04.110
- But the algae is fine, right?
- We won't lose it?


01:08:04.240 --> 01:08:05.373
The algae is fine.


01:08:07.072 --> 01:08:10.905
That, on the other hand?


01:08:11.036 --> 01:08:12.867
If we fly down...


01:08:16.962 --> 01:08:20.708
These people need our help.


01:08:20.838 --> 01:08:23.845
Come on.


01:08:23.976 --> 01:08:26.546
Wait, Hannah. Wait.


01:08:26.676 --> 01:08:28.856
- Stop.
- What the fuck, dude?


01:08:28.987 --> 01:08:31.512
He's right. He's right.


01:08:31.644 --> 01:08:34.171
Please.


01:08:34.301 --> 01:08:35.957
Start loading
the mother cultures.


01:08:36.088 --> 01:08:38.353
We're leaving tomorrow.


01:08:38.484 --> 01:08:39.922
I'll prepare the Vesta.


01:08:40.052 --> 01:08:41.272
Hannah.


01:08:43.842 --> 01:08:45.280
Hannah!


01:09:01.922 --> 01:09:03.097
Shit.


01:09:03.228 --> 01:09:06.103
Come on.


01:09:17.867 --> 01:09:19.436
Again?


01:09:19.567 --> 01:09:21.614
In case you didn't know this,
I...


01:09:21.745 --> 01:09:23.619
I just killed us.
So, yeah.


01:09:23.750 --> 01:09:25.927
- Yeah.
- Yeah, but the other eight times


01:09:26.057 --> 01:09:27.625
you made it.


01:09:30.937 --> 01:09:33.464
You're just getting tired,
that's all.


01:09:36.295 --> 01:09:39.040
This flight course that you
gave me is fucking narrow.


01:09:39.170 --> 01:09:42.220
Well, then they're lucky that
it's you sitting in the seat.


01:09:48.537 --> 01:09:52.284
Hannah, I really think
we should talk about the...


01:09:52.415 --> 01:09:54.113
About all this.


01:09:54.244 --> 01:09:55.813
What does this mean now?


01:09:55.943 --> 01:09:58.687
Nothing. This means nothing.


01:10:00.386 --> 01:10:03.699
Hannah.


01:10:03.830 --> 01:10:06.051
Isn't it... likely that...


01:10:06.182 --> 01:10:07.706
Stop it, okay! I...


01:10:07.837 --> 01:10:11.366
No! Fuck.


01:10:11.496 --> 01:10:13.806
I'm going to lose it
at reentry or landing


01:10:13.937 --> 01:10:15.593
or without the station's
radiation shield.


01:10:15.723 --> 01:10:18.728
Okay, that's...
That's super fucked up, yeah.


01:10:22.083 --> 01:10:25.917
I'm sorry. I-I didn't mean to...


01:10:26.048 --> 01:10:27.441
It has no chance anyway.


01:10:27.573 --> 01:10:31.973
I mean, even if we stayed,
I can't raise a baby here.


01:10:32.103 --> 01:10:34.978
Just you, me, and Dimitri?


01:10:36.852 --> 01:10:38.419
This changes nothing.
It just makes


01:10:38.549 --> 01:10:40.466
the whole situation shittier.


01:10:44.258 --> 01:10:47.003
I'm sorry.


01:10:47.133 --> 01:10:48.834
I really am.


01:10:54.627 --> 01:10:59.637
Look, this one probably
doesn't have a chance.


01:10:59.768 --> 01:11:01.684
But when we're down there...


01:11:01.815 --> 01:11:04.386
Are you saying you want
a baby with me?


01:11:07.740 --> 01:11:11.051
Why not?


01:11:11.181 --> 01:11:13.272
I mean, imagine.


01:11:13.403 --> 01:11:18.239
It could kick butt.
My brains, your muscles.


01:11:18.370 --> 01:11:21.419
Yeah.


01:11:21.549 --> 01:11:23.075
Yeah, you're right. I'm...


01:11:23.205 --> 01:11:25.688
I'm definitely too tired
for this.


01:11:27.867 --> 01:11:30.743
Eight landings out of ten
must be enough, right?


01:12:23.240 --> 01:12:25.941
Okay. Bring me the last one.


01:12:29.122 --> 01:12:33.434
This is really enough
for 300 people?


01:12:33.566 --> 01:12:37.702
- Yep.
- That's the minimum amount.


01:12:37.833 --> 01:12:41.233
What? Wait, again, you think
I'm tricking you or something?


01:12:47.854 --> 01:12:50.338
It's just you've not said
one word of resistance


01:12:50.468 --> 01:12:51.688
the whole day.


01:12:51.818 --> 01:12:54.258
What do you want from me?


01:12:54.388 --> 01:12:57.655
You think I'm stupid enough to
fly down with algae cultures


01:12:57.787 --> 01:12:59.224
that don't work?


01:12:59.355 --> 01:13:03.581
Well, I can't stay here
without you two, so...


01:13:03.712 --> 01:13:07.023
You won. Congratulations.


01:13:07.153 --> 01:13:08.764
What else do you want from me?


01:13:18.437 --> 01:13:21.748
Okay. All checks are done.


01:13:21.878 --> 01:13:23.579
Are you ready for this?


01:13:25.452 --> 01:13:27.412
Nope.


01:13:27.542 --> 01:13:28.893
Perfect.


01:13:29.024 --> 01:13:31.768
<i>Vesta 1,
flight corridor received.</i>


01:13:31.898 --> 01:13:35.820
Central Nibra, contacting you
again in 92 minutes.


01:13:35.951 --> 01:13:38.476
<i>- Okay.
- We wish you a safe journey</i>


01:13:38.608 --> 01:13:40.961
<i>and we're looking forward...</i>


01:13:41.092 --> 01:13:43.270
And the contact windows
just passed.


01:13:43.400 --> 01:13:46.494
Okay. Closing the inner door.


01:13:54.292 --> 01:13:55.816
Uh... What is that?


01:13:57.691 --> 01:13:59.390
The jets are not responding.


01:14:05.402 --> 01:14:06.839
Whoa.


01:14:10.847 --> 01:14:13.548
What... What is that?


01:14:13.679 --> 01:14:17.382
- Check tank's overheated, but...
- we haven't even ignited.


01:14:17.513 --> 01:14:18.733
Overheated?


01:14:18.864 --> 01:14:20.694
The temperature, it's rising,
but fuck,


01:14:20.823 --> 01:14:22.565
this can't be right.


01:14:22.696 --> 01:14:25.050
- Hannah? What?
- We have overpressure.


01:14:25.181 --> 01:14:26.879
- Oh, shit.
- Makes no sense!


01:14:27.009 --> 01:14:28.578
I need to release the tanks.


01:14:30.670 --> 01:14:33.631
- Did it work?!
- The valves are not opening.


01:14:33.761 --> 01:14:36.027
- Try the gas outlet!
- I tried.


01:14:36.159 --> 01:14:38.772
They must have deformed
under the heat.


01:14:38.903 --> 01:14:40.864
How hot are the tanks?


01:14:42.824 --> 01:14:44.871
Hannah?


01:14:45.003 --> 01:14:46.224
Hannah!


01:14:46.354 --> 01:14:48.837
- Unfasten immediately.
- Get out now!


01:14:54.717 --> 01:14:55.938
Come on!


01:14:56.068 --> 01:14:57.637
- Come on, come on, come o.
- Come on.


01:14:57.768 --> 01:15:00.469
- Come on, we're gonna explode!
- Put yourself together!


01:15:00.600 --> 01:15:02.080
You put yourself together!


01:15:02.211 --> 01:15:03.300
Come on!


01:15:13.451 --> 01:15:15.542
- Fuck.
- What?


01:15:15.672 --> 01:15:20.814
Look. The Vesta's cooling system
shut down almost 11 hours ago.


01:15:20.944 --> 01:15:22.557
That's why the tanks overheated.


01:15:22.687 --> 01:15:24.212
I'll redirect the solar panels.


01:15:24.342 --> 01:15:25.911
Shadow alone won't do it
anymore.


01:15:26.041 --> 01:15:28.785
Look at the temperature.
We need to decouple it.


01:15:28.916 --> 01:15:30.005
What? No. No.


01:15:30.135 --> 01:15:31.576
There has to be another way.


01:15:31.706 --> 01:15:33.710
We can dump the tanks manually.


01:15:33.841 --> 01:15:35.625
That... That could work.


01:15:35.757 --> 01:15:38.284
Only from inside the vesse,
but that's far too dangerous.


01:15:39.939 --> 01:15:42.118
Gavin, stop!
It could blow up any second.


01:15:42.249 --> 01:15:43.600
Fuck!


01:15:53.314 --> 01:15:54.859
He has to go through
the whole cooling block.


01:15:54.883 --> 01:15:57.888
It's impossible.
He's killing himself.


01:15:58.018 --> 01:15:59.587
All of us.


01:16:01.896 --> 01:16:03.508
Can you still decouple?


01:16:12.831 --> 01:16:14.200
- No, no, no! No!
- Wait, wait, wait! Hannah!


01:16:14.224 --> 01:16:16.753
No! No! No! No!


01:16:16.883 --> 01:16:19.235
No! Wait! Stop!


01:16:19.366 --> 01:16:21.676
Stop!


01:16:24.725 --> 01:16:26.817
No! No!


01:16:26.948 --> 01:16:29.691
Hannah, please!


01:16:29.822 --> 01:16:31.783
No!


01:16:31.913 --> 01:16:34.004
No!


01:17:45.583 --> 01:17:47.107
I had to.


01:18:40.172 --> 01:18:41.827
You did the right thing,
Commander.


01:18:45.051 --> 01:18:46.968
He would have died.


01:18:50.148 --> 01:18:55.462
I know it doesn't seem
like much up here,


01:18:55.593 --> 01:18:57.815
but, uh...


01:18:57.946 --> 01:19:01.300
This place saved our lives.


01:19:05.875 --> 01:19:07.355
It could be home.


01:19:15.111 --> 01:19:16.548
How was it for you?


01:19:20.382 --> 01:19:21.906
Having a child?


01:19:31.361 --> 01:19:32.929
Loud.


01:19:35.631 --> 01:19:39.420
Nerve-wracking. Exhausting.


01:19:42.079 --> 01:19:43.603
Amazing.


01:19:47.960 --> 01:19:50.398
You can't possibly imagine
loving anyone


01:19:50.529 --> 01:19:53.754
like you love
this little creature.


01:20:03.295 --> 01:20:04.819
Okay.


01:20:35.446 --> 01:20:38.147
We don't need two people
to tell them.


01:20:38.278 --> 01:20:39.890
- But I was...
- Go.


01:20:40.021 --> 01:20:41.545
Or I go.


01:20:49.475 --> 01:20:51.391
Did you do it
because of the pregnancy?


01:20:54.353 --> 01:20:56.270
No.


01:20:56.401 --> 01:20:57.751
I did it because of us.


01:21:00.149 --> 01:21:02.283
<i>Vesta 1?</i>


01:21:02.414 --> 01:21:05.246
<i>Vesta 1, we can't
detect your signal.</i>


01:21:05.376 --> 01:21:10.212
<i>Do you read? Vesta 1?</i>


01:21:10.343 --> 01:21:11.737
Yes, Esther. We're here.


01:21:11.868 --> 01:21:14.263
<i>- Gavin. Where are you?
- What happened?</i>


01:21:35.218 --> 01:21:36.917
What's Icarus?


01:21:39.618 --> 01:21:41.405
They said that you would know.


01:21:54.083 --> 01:21:56.305
My actual mission.


01:21:56.435 --> 01:21:58.917
Once I found
a working mother culture,


01:21:59.049 --> 01:22:01.359
I was to bring down
the entire algae lab.


01:22:03.318 --> 01:22:06.892
It can be ejected and flown
on separately.


01:22:07.022 --> 01:22:08.023
What?


01:22:08.111 --> 01:22:10.245
It was a secret
military operation.


01:22:10.376 --> 01:22:12.206
Surprised these CEOs
even knew about it.


01:22:12.337 --> 01:22:14.166
Wait, wait, wait.


01:22:14.297 --> 01:22:16.431
C-Can we go down with it?


01:22:17.956 --> 01:22:20.874
It's not made for passengers
and can't be steered.


01:22:21.005 --> 01:22:24.012
Without Navicon, we can only
detach it at a calculated moment


01:22:24.143 --> 01:22:27.062
and hope for the best.


01:22:27.192 --> 01:22:29.849
But theoretically,
we could board it


01:22:29.980 --> 01:22:32.071
if we adapted it for passengers.


01:22:34.817 --> 01:22:36.647
Hannah. What the fuck?
Why didn't you tell me


01:22:36.778 --> 01:22:38.278
that there was
another chance for reentry?


01:22:38.302 --> 01:22:41.091
Because it's not
a serious option, okay?


01:22:51.720 --> 01:22:54.639
Three people against 300.


01:22:58.996 --> 01:23:03.831
Yes. Or even more
if other bunkers made it.


01:23:10.061 --> 01:23:11.802
I think we should do it.


01:23:11.934 --> 01:23:14.287
If we don't try, then it's done
for them down there.


01:23:14.418 --> 01:23:16.596
We can't let that happen.


01:23:16.726 --> 01:23:19.210
This is bigger than us, right?


01:23:23.175 --> 01:23:24.700
Right?


01:24:45.209 --> 01:24:47.300
You asshole, disconnected
the Vesta


01:24:47.431 --> 01:24:50.131
from the cooling cycle.


01:24:50.262 --> 01:24:52.222
We almost died because of you.


01:24:55.230 --> 01:24:58.062
I didn't want... I just...


01:24:58.192 --> 01:25:00.893
I just wanted to delay.


01:25:01.023 --> 01:25:02.243
It was an accident.


01:25:05.076 --> 01:25:07.558
I-I didn't know the valves
can close up.


01:25:07.688 --> 01:25:10.347
I couldn't let what happened
to Danilo happen to us.


01:25:10.478 --> 01:25:12.569
Bullshit!


01:25:12.699 --> 01:25:15.750
You just did it because
you're a selfish coward.


01:25:24.854 --> 01:25:27.294
You know what this is?


01:25:27.425 --> 01:25:29.210
Yeah.


01:25:29.340 --> 01:25:31.345
And you know what it does?


01:25:31.476 --> 01:25:34.350
I found out at some point, yes.


01:25:34.482 --> 01:25:37.924
Good, 'cause that's what
we will do now.


01:25:38.055 --> 01:25:40.101
We will pump back
the symbiosis cultures in here


01:25:40.232 --> 01:25:43.065
and we will fly down.


01:25:43.195 --> 01:25:47.247
So y-you knew about Icarus
all of this time


01:25:47.377 --> 01:25:48.991
and you didn't say anything?


01:25:56.395 --> 01:25:58.749
You didn't want this either...


01:26:00.839 --> 01:26:02.495
did you?


01:26:02.625 --> 01:26:07.549
- Gavin is right.
- We need to help.


01:26:07.680 --> 01:26:13.125
There's no shame in caring
for your own life, Hannah.


01:26:13.255 --> 01:26:14.823
Especially now.


01:26:14.954 --> 01:26:16.218
Stop it.


01:26:21.010 --> 01:26:22.665
Have you ever asked yourself


01:26:22.796 --> 01:26:27.109
why Nibra needed the algae
so bad all of a sudden?


01:26:27.240 --> 01:26:29.681
For years, they didn't
give a fuck.


01:26:29.812 --> 01:26:32.206
Suddenly, they want
everything now.


01:26:32.337 --> 01:26:33.732
They need the system now.


01:26:33.862 --> 01:26:35.649
They send you to space
to get it.


01:26:35.779 --> 01:26:38.437
Why? Why now?


01:26:38.569 --> 01:26:42.010
What are you trying to say?


01:26:42.140 --> 01:26:43.621
They knew.


01:26:47.281 --> 01:26:52.073
They knew
a catastrophe was coming.


01:26:52.204 --> 01:26:55.819
They just didn't tell anyone.
I mean, why would they?


01:26:55.950 --> 01:26:59.130
They didn't want
to share their bunkers.


01:27:01.963 --> 01:27:07.626
You really think they would
give you their algae


01:27:07.756 --> 01:27:09.324
if it was the other way around?


01:27:21.829 --> 01:27:23.484
We've made a decision.


01:27:23.615 --> 01:27:27.230
<i>We're sending the algae lab
down to you like you asked.</i>


01:27:27.361 --> 01:27:29.801
But we're coming with it.


01:27:29.932 --> 01:27:33.242
Okay, we're looking
forward to that.


01:27:33.373 --> 01:27:35.987
- Wait.
- One more thing before we start.


01:27:36.118 --> 01:27:38.513
I-I need to talk
to one of the soldiers.


01:27:40.736 --> 01:27:43.960
<i>But I am our representative.</i>


01:27:44.090 --> 01:27:47.444
Yes, but Icarus
is a military mission, so...


01:27:47.575 --> 01:27:51.061
<i>Okay.</i>


01:27:53.065 --> 01:27:57.595
<i>They say...
there are no soldiers here.</i>


01:28:01.735 --> 01:28:04.611
But you said the soldiers
brought you into the bunkers.


01:28:06.701 --> 01:28:12.059
<i>- Yes, they brought us here.
- But... we have limited space.</i>


01:28:12.190 --> 01:28:16.853
<i>We have room for 300 civilians,
families.</i>


01:28:16.983 --> 01:28:18.987
So what, you...


01:28:19.118 --> 01:28:23.736
You just left them outside...
to die?


01:28:23.867 --> 01:28:25.434
<i>They did their duty.</i>


01:28:27.743 --> 01:28:29.355
That was Nibra's order...


01:28:29.486 --> 01:28:32.535
for all evacuation soldiers?


01:28:32.666 --> 01:28:36.108
<i>Hannah, it's your job
to keep us alive.</i>


01:28:36.239 --> 01:28:38.330
You lied!


01:28:38.460 --> 01:28:41.030
<i>No, we didn't lie.</i>


01:28:41.162 --> 01:28:45.430
<i>You just assumed
what you wanted to believe.</i>


01:28:45.561 --> 01:28:48.873
<i>I'm sorry,
but what were you thinking?</i>


01:28:53.361 --> 01:28:56.453
<i>All we want is to live.
Nothing more.</i>


01:28:56.584 --> 01:28:59.155
<i>We want our kids to survive.</i>


01:28:59.286 --> 01:29:02.204
<i>I mean,
you can't blame us for that.</i>


01:29:11.570 --> 01:29:13.095
Fuck!


01:29:15.448 --> 01:29:17.583
Fuck!


01:29:20.545 --> 01:29:21.764
No!


01:29:34.877 --> 01:29:36.751
- Come on.
- Get off the floor.


01:29:36.882 --> 01:29:38.582
No. I'm done.


01:29:38.713 --> 01:29:41.152
Hannah, they'll run out
of oxygen within days.


01:29:41.283 --> 01:29:44.898
Yeah. And why would
cannon fodder like me care?


01:29:45.029 --> 01:29:47.687
They didn't give a shit
about me or Knopf.


01:29:47.818 --> 01:29:49.604
Or my parents.


01:29:51.607 --> 01:29:53.089
Apparently money and privilege


01:29:53.220 --> 01:29:54.918
don't get you a spot
in the bunker either.


01:29:57.445 --> 01:30:01.453
You know that there are children
down there, too, right?


01:30:01.584 --> 01:30:03.283
And what about this one?


01:30:05.113 --> 01:30:07.291
You said that we couldn't
raise it here.


01:30:07.422 --> 01:30:08.859
Why actually not?


01:30:08.990 --> 01:30:12.781
I mean, this place is better
than anywhere I lived before.


01:30:12.911 --> 01:30:15.133
Growing old here?


01:30:15.264 --> 01:30:16.657
Never seeing earth?


01:30:16.788 --> 01:30:19.750
What kind of a life is that?


01:30:19.881 --> 01:30:21.537
At least a life.


01:30:28.291 --> 01:30:32.516
- I-I don't get it.
- A-Are you just hurt?


01:30:32.648 --> 01:30:36.958
- Would you really want this baby?
- See, I don't know, okay?


01:30:37.090 --> 01:30:39.530
I never thought
about having a child.


01:30:39.661 --> 01:30:42.318
Having family meant going back
to being poor.


01:30:42.448 --> 01:30:44.453
Not obeying meant being poor.


01:30:44.584 --> 01:30:47.893
A soldier doesn't
even have that choice.


01:30:48.024 --> 01:30:49.942
And that choice is more
important than saving


01:30:50.073 --> 01:30:52.120
the rest of our world?


01:30:52.251 --> 01:30:54.082
Yes.


01:30:54.212 --> 01:30:56.912
You wouldn't
understand that, domer.


01:30:57.043 --> 01:31:01.095
For someone like you, it's easy
playing "Save the World."


01:31:01.225 --> 01:31:03.598
But not everyone has a daddy who
sends him up here for safety


01:31:03.622 --> 01:31:05.408
if everything else
goes down the drain.


01:31:08.152 --> 01:31:09.763
Is that really what you think?


01:31:13.947 --> 01:31:15.341
Hmm.


01:32:20.995 --> 01:32:22.911
Gavin?


01:32:47.745 --> 01:32:49.182
Open the door!


01:32:53.625 --> 01:32:56.108
I'm finishing what we started.


01:32:56.239 --> 01:32:57.982
Are you leaving me behind?


01:32:58.113 --> 01:33:01.685
No, but I... I just need
to finish up. Just wait.


01:33:01.816 --> 01:33:03.385
How can you know
I won't stop you?


01:33:06.564 --> 01:33:09.353
Because you're a good person.


01:33:09.484 --> 01:33:11.052
And you know that this is right.


01:34:48.161 --> 01:34:49.771
Hannah, don't! Stop!


01:34:51.645 --> 01:34:53.432
- Gavin, stop!
- Please!


01:34:53.563 --> 01:34:54.826
No!


01:35:01.403 --> 01:35:02.710
Stop it!


01:35:02.841 --> 01:35:04.279
What led you to do this?!


01:35:25.583 --> 01:35:29.243
Hannah, can...
Can we talk about this? I...


01:35:29.373 --> 01:35:32.118
I can't.


01:35:32.249 --> 01:35:35.429
I just don't want to.


01:35:35.559 --> 01:35:36.997
Hannah, please j...


01:35:46.145 --> 01:35:48.149
Fuck!


01:36:00.349 --> 01:36:02.397
Hannah, you can fix this, right?


01:36:04.226 --> 01:36:05.490
Hannah?


01:36:05.620 --> 01:36:08.496
I'm sorry.


01:36:08.626 --> 01:36:10.412
I want to stay.


01:38:46.682 --> 01:38:48.077
Gavin?


01:38:55.047 --> 01:38:56.572
Gavin?


01:41:44.388 --> 01:41:46.304
Come on.


01:41:46.436 --> 01:41:49.964
Let's see if we can
fix Icarus somehow.


01:41:50.095 --> 01:41:54.277
Yeah. W... What?


01:41:56.717 --> 01:42:00.420
We need three breathers
or the gas mix collapses.


01:42:00.550 --> 01:42:02.076
Your words.


01:42:07.129 --> 01:42:12.357
But... You...
You think Gavin did it...


01:42:12.488 --> 01:42:14.101
Yeah.


01:42:14.232 --> 01:42:17.105
He forced his will on us.


01:42:17.236 --> 01:42:18.675
He got what he wanted.


01:42:23.292 --> 01:42:24.992
Oh.


01:42:26.777 --> 01:42:30.263
- What?
- No, no, no.


01:42:33.399 --> 01:42:35.187
We need three breathers, right?


01:42:37.756 --> 01:42:39.193
Oh, God.


01:42:44.596 --> 01:42:47.297
Dimitri.


01:42:47.427 --> 01:42:50.782
I certainly definitely tried...
I-I just didn't want him


01:42:50.912 --> 01:42:53.744
to hurt himself.


01:42:58.145 --> 01:42:59.583
I wanted to save him.


01:43:08.558 --> 01:43:09.777
Stop.


01:43:09.908 --> 01:43:12.434
- I'm sorry. I didn't...
- Okay, just stop.


01:43:40.359 --> 01:43:42.582
Come on!


01:43:42.713 --> 01:43:43.933
- No!
- No, no, no.


01:43:47.114 --> 01:43:49.118
Now, now, I got you.


01:43:50.903 --> 01:43:53.212
- Let's go.
- Let's go.


01:43:53.343 --> 01:43:55.783
- Okay.
- No!


01:43:55.914 --> 01:43:58.571
- Let's go.
- Come on.


01:44:05.236 --> 01:44:07.153
Good night. Yes.


01:44:56.687 --> 01:44:58.516
<i>Hello, hello?</i>


01:44:58.648 --> 01:45:03.266
<i>Is there anyone?
Hello? Hello?</i>


01:45:03.397 --> 01:45:05.095
<i>- Hello?
- Look, guys!</i>


01:45:05.227 --> 01:45:07.579
<i>- The thing is working.
- Hey, give it to me!</i>


01:45:07.709 --> 01:45:10.105
- Hello?
- Are you in there?


01:45:10.236 --> 01:45:11.500
In the box?


01:45:11.630 --> 01:45:14.766
<i>- No.
- We're in the southern camps.</i>


01:45:14.897 --> 01:45:16.510
<i>And you?
What's your name?</i>


01:45:16.640 --> 01:45:18.994
<i>- Knopf.
- Knopf.</i>


01:45:19.124 --> 01:45:21.738
<i>- Where are you?
- Eh, Rubikon.</i>


01:45:21.870 --> 01:45:24.657
<i>Can you play outside there
again, too?</i>


01:45:24.788 --> 01:45:28.142
- No.
- Mom says we can't live outside.


01:45:28.273 --> 01:45:30.451
<i>So he must still be
somewhere up north.</i>


01:45:30.581 --> 01:45:32.629
<i>- Hey, shh.
- Well, then ask her</i>


01:45:32.759 --> 01:45:34.503
<i>if you can come down here.</i>


01:45:34.634 --> 01:45:35.916
<i>The grown ups are always
searching for survivors anyway.</i>


01:45:35.940 --> 01:45:37.508
<i>They say that
we must help each other</i>


01:45:37.639 --> 01:45:39.513
<i>because everything
is different now.</i>


01:45:39.644 --> 01:45:40.994
<i>Stop it!</i>


01:45:41.125 --> 01:45:43.085
<i>Seriously. Can't you come?</i>

